# GRADUATED from known_gaps/ — Track B (round MEMORY SAFETY / ONE OWNERSHIP
# BOUNDARY, 2026-08-06). Guarded by `security_safe` in tests/security.rs.
#
# CELL: Guard[String].get() → Dict.put · TEMP form · payload String · backend C
#
# Before Track B's fix: this program aborted with `AddressSanitizer:
# attempting double-free`, exit 134 (both backends). `g.get()` yields a View
# into the mutex-owned payload; the consumer's AST-shape guard at
# `ensure_owned_at_consuming_arg` (`src/ir/lowering/context.rs:2680`) skipped
# the borrow-detection predicate for the expression-temp arm, so the temp's
# View tag was discarded and the shallow Str header was memcpy'd into the map
# slot as an ALIAS. Scope-exit freed both ends of the alias.
#
# After Track B: the else arm reads the same View/borrow accessors as the
# identifier arm; the temp is cloned before the callee memcpy's it; the
# collection owns an independent buffer and the mutex still owns its own.
#
# INTENDED: exit 0, prints `1`.
#
# HEAP-FORCED VALUE (never a literal — a rodata String has cap=0, so
# `gorget_string_free` short-circuits and the bug reads as absent on the
# pre-fix compiler).

String heaped():
    return "hello " + "world" + "-forced"

void main():
    Mutex[String] m = Mutex[String](heaped())
    Guard[String] g = m.lock()
    Dict[String, String] d = {}
    d.put("k", g.get())
    print(d.len())
